# squawk-feed settings.conf - TRACKED EXAMPLE (sovereign-projects).
# Runtime copy: ~/.fleet-bus/squawk-relay/settings.conf (mode 0600, NOT tracked).
# Copy this file there to start, then add keys as needed.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE lines. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Values may be wrapped in single or double quotes (stripped on load).
# Real environment variables ALWAYS win over this file.
# A missing settings file is fine - the server starts without it.
# CLI: --settings-file PATH, or $SQUAWK_FEED_SETTINGS to override the path.
#
# --- Token (usually NOT needed) -------------------------------------------
# The server configures its bearer token by itself, in this order:
#   1. $SQUAWK_FEED_TOKEN env var
#   2. token file (~/.fleet-bus/squawk-relay/feed-token,
#      or --token-file / $SQUAWK_FEED_TOKEN_FILE)
#   3. secure auto-generate (secrets.token_urlsafe(32)), persisted 0600
# Only set SQUAWK_FEED_TOKEN here for a fixed token; env var still wins.
#SQUAWK_FEED_TOKEN=
#
# --- Future keys ------------------------------------------------------------
# Add integration/provider keys here as needed. Loaded into the process
# environment at startup; existing env vars take precedence.
#SQUAWK_FEED_EXTRA_KEY=
